speaker: Aadi Bajpai
---
bio:

Aadi is an open-source maintainer and contributor, Google Summer of Code mentor, and Google Code-in winner—all done while also being a high school student. He loves automating things and hates writing about himself in the third person.

---
title: Automating Away the Open-Source Maintenance Burden
---
abstract:

As a solo developer on an open-source project, how do you avoid issues piling up, boring maintenance tasks and burnout? In this talk, we see how we can assert dominance over all of that by automating away the boring and ushering in a sense of freedom by minimizing effort and maximizing productivity.
